  - [1mCorrupt or stale stored JSON[0m: a [38;5;153mschemaVersion[39m key on the payload. Parse failure or version mismatch reseeds rather
    than throwing — a bad write in development shouldn't leave you with an app that won't boot and no obvious way back.
  - [1mDangling references[0m (an event or follower pointing at an id that no longer exists): filtered out at read time, not
    treated as an error. Derivation should be total over whatever the log contains.

  [1mTesting[0m

  The derivation logic is pure, so the valuable tests are cheap. The ones that matter: self-authored changes never
  appear in your own inbox; a new follower sees prior history; an unassigned user keeps the notification that told them
  so; read state survives a reload; unread count matches the inbox length; log pruning drops oldest first and takes
  orphaned read entries with it. Plus one structural test on the store — [1mevery mutation appends exactly one event[0m —
  which is the invariant the whole design rests on.

  [1mTooling[0m

  No build config exists yet, so this is the cheapest moment to decide. I'd keep the app as plain ES modules with no
  bundler — [38;5;153mindex.html[39m keeps working off a static server — and add a [38;5;153mpackage.json[39m only to host the dev tooling.
